{"diagnosis": "Fetch fails with `TRAP: cpu trap asserted` and `FAIL 0xdead` instead of clean NOP progress. `mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle` at picorv32.v:384 selects `mem_rdata_q` when `mem_xfer` is true and live `mem_rdata` when idle, which is inverted. This feeds stale/previous-cycle data into `mem_rdata_latched` (picorv32.v:386-388) causing illegal decode and trap.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -384,1 +384,1 @@
-	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata_q : mem_rdata;
+	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata : mem_rdata_q;
", "expected": "tohost PASS with no `TRAP: cpu trap asserted`, checksum != c2a7a4d6295484feeb9ec1ea9381732b8e39a7ccd1997c7d70f6454da2fb4659"}

